==============================================================================
A1  Well-definedness of the moves on types mod 3*2^k
==============================================================================
Claim F: T(n) mod 3*2^(k-1) is a function of n mod 3*2^k.
Claim D: 2n mod 3*2^(k+1) is a function of n mod 3*2^k (injective, image = even classes).
Claim E: for n = 2 mod 3, E(n) mod 2^(k+1) is a function of n mod 3*2^k; the map is a
         bijection onto the odd classes mod 2^(k+1); E(n) mod 3 is NOT a function of
         n mod 3*2^k: the three lifts mod 9*2^k give E(n) = 0,1,2 mod 3 once each.
Claim E': E(n) mod 3*2^j is a function of n mod 9*2^(j-1) (j >= 1), and not of n mod 3*2^k for any k.
  verified for both sheets, k = 1..10 (Claims F, D, E) and j = 1..8 (Claim E'),
  six lifts per class.  In particular E(n) mod 192 needs n mod 288 = 9*32, D(n) mod 192
  needs n mod 96, and T(n) mod 96 needs n mod 192.

