A2  The owner's inverse-tree type automaton A_k at modulus 3*2^k; k = 6 (192) in detail
==============================================================================
States Z/3*2^k.  Edges:  r -D-> 2r mod 3*2^k  (every r);
                         r -E-> s  for the three s with s = (2r-1)/3 mod 2^k   (r = 2 mod 3).
The E-edge is nondeterministic exactly in the mod-3 digit (A1, Claim E); each of the three
targets carries Haar weight 1/3.  This is a sound over-approximation: m in T^-1(n) implies
type(m) in delta(type(n)).

