A_6 (modulus 192):
  SCCs: one of size 128 = the 128 non-multiples of 3 (2-part free, mod-3 part in {1,2}),
        and 64 singletons = the multiples of 3; only {0} carries a loop (D(0) = 0).
  Condensation: big SCC --E(choice 0 mod 3)--> odd multiples of 3 --D-chain--> 0 (sink).
  Steps to reach 0 inside the multiples of 3 (D is nilpotent on the 2-part mod 64): {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 2, 3: 4, 4: 8, 5: 16, 6: 32}
  Every one of the 192 types is reachable from the root types {1, 2}.
  Out-degree census (with multiplicity): {1: 128, 4: 64}   (64 branch states r = 2 mod 3 have D + 3 E-choices)
  Weighted matrix (D weight 1, each E-choice 1/3): mean row sum = 1.333333 = 4/3;
  spectral radius = 1.333333333333 = 4/3; on the core the Perron vector is 1 on r = 1 mod 3 and 4/3 on r = 2 mod 3
  (solves 3L^2 - L - 4 = 0, roots 4/3 and -1); leading core eigenvalues: +1.333333+0.000000i, -1.000000+0.000000i, +0.002250+0.000000i, +0.001123+0.001948i
  Pruned branching (children that are not multiples of 3): from r = 1 mod 3: 1 (the D-child);
  from r = 2 mod 3: 1 + 2/3; average over the core 4/3.  Probability that an E-child is a leaf: 1/3.

  Forward automaton on Z/192 (r -> T(r) mod 192, two choices of the top bit): one SCC of the
  128 non-multiples of 3 and 64 singleton SCCs (the multiples of 3; only 0 carries a loop, T(0) = 0).
  The core never enters 3Z: after the first odd step an orbit never meets 3Z again.  So 3Z is a
  SOURCE region forward and a SINK region backward: the leaf cones of the inverse tree.

==============================================================================
A3  Finite-level shadows of the generators and of the root at modulus 192
==============================================================================
  D: fixed type 0 and the 2-cycle {64, 128} (the 2-part is nilpotent, the mod-3 digit swaps 1<->2).
     Real meaning: 0 is the fixed point of D; deep D-chains of a multiple of 3 end in type 0.
  E: the type 191 = -1 mod 192 has an E-self-loop, E(-1) = -1 exactly (E's fixed point is -1).
  S: every sibling ladder p, 4p+1, 16p+5, ... ends in the 3-cycle {21, 85, 149} mod 192:
     all three residues mod 3 of -1/3 mod 64 (3*21+1 = 64).  S^j(p) -> -1/3 in Z_2, and -1/3 = E(0).
  Root: 1 -D-> 2 -E-> 1 is a 2-cycle of A_6 (the cycle {1,2} of T).
  Trunk (4^i-1)/3 = E D^(2i-1)(1) = S^(i-1)(1) mod 192: [1, 5, 21, 85, 149, 21, 85, 149, 21] ... (enters {21,85,149} at i = 3).

==============================================================================
A4  What a residue mod 192 decides
==============================================================================
  For every r mod 192 and both sheets (59 lifts each):
   * n mod 64 decides the parity window (x_0, ..., x_5) of the T-orbit (Terras; a bijection Z/64 -> {0,1}^6);
   * n mod 192 decides the mod-3 types of T^0(n), ..., T^6(n): after the first odd step the type is
     2 at an odd-step image and alternates 1,2 along halvings; before it, it is 2^(-j) n mod 3;
   * n mod 192 decides T^6(n) mod 3^(1+a), a = #odd steps in the window, and not mod 3^(2+a);
   * backward: n mod 192 decides D(n) mod 384 and, for n = 2 mod 3, E(n) mod 128, but not E(n) mod 3.
  Read on a tree node m = w(root): m mod 64 is the LAST six moves of its path (E = odd, D = even),
  m mod 3 is its own branching type.  So the owner's type is: one branching trit + a six-move window.
  #classes mod 192 by odd steps a in the window: {0: 3, 1: 18, 2: 45, 3: 60, 4: 45, 5: 18, 6: 3} = 3*C(6,a).

==============================================================================
A5  Order relations inside the 6-step window: exact gate bound and census, both sheets
==============================================================================
For a window x_i -> x_j (j-i = m <= 6) with a odd steps: 2^m x_j = 3^a x_i + b*c, c >= 0 (c = 0 iff a = 0).
Word prediction: x_j > x_i iff 3^a > 2^m.  A crossing (actual order != prediction) needs
x_i < gate = c/|2^m - 3^a| on the side where b*c and 2^m - 3^a have the same sign.
  sheet b=+1: largest gate over all words of length <= 6 = 76/5 = 15.2000 at (m, word) = (5, (0, 0, 1, 1, 1))
  sheet b=-1: largest gate over all words of length <= 6 = 260/17 = 15.2941 at (m, word) = (6, (0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1))
  sheet b=+1: n <= 10^6 with a non-generic comparison inside the window T^0..T^6: 9 starts, 37 windows (equalities at cycle points included); starts = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 10, 16, 32]
  sheet b=-1: n <= 10^6 with a non-generic comparison inside the window T^0..T^6: 21 starts, 111 windows (equalities at cycle points included); starts = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, 16, 19, 20, 27, 28, 32, 40, 56, 80]
  PROVED: every value in the window is >= n/64 (each step at least halves), so for n > 64*76/5 (plus)
  resp. n > 64*260/17 (minus), i.e. for every n > 979, the full order pattern of (T^0 n, ..., T^6 n)
  is the word's generic pattern: a function of n mod 64, the same on both sheets after r -> -r.
  The census shows the true exceptions are the listed starts (all <= 32 plus, <= 80 minus).
  (Consistent with the order-laws note: short-lag genericity; the first sheet-separating window
  has 12 odd steps, far beyond the 6 steps a residue mod 192 sees.)

==============================================================================
A6  The owner's dictionary: siblings, the 4x recursion and the hidden choice
==============================================================================
  T^-1(n) = {2n} U {(2n-1)/3 : n = 2 mod 3} (brute force n <= 1000, identity n <= 20000).
  E D^2 = S E with S(p) = 4p+1 on every legal x in [-3000, 3000] (identity: (8x-1)/3 = 4(2x-1)/3 + 1).
  U(4p+1) = U(p), v_2(3S(p)+1) = v_2(3p+1)+2 and 3S^j(p)+1 = 4^j(3p+1) (odd p < 20000):
  the siblings converge 2-adically to -1/3 = E(0), whose T-image is 0 = D's fixed point.
  For N = 1 mod 3 (N <= 30000): (4N-1)/3 = 4*(N-1)/3 + 1, consecutive rungs of one sibling ladder.
   N even (5000 cases): (N-1)/3 = E(N/2) is odd, a genuine T-predecessor of N/2; the 'A/2 branch'.
   N odd  (5000 cases): (N-1)/3 is EVEN; it is the phantom rung j = -1, and the arrow
          (N-1)/3 -> 3*(N-1)/3 + 1 = N is exactly the extra arrow of the E-graph relaxation.
  So the owner's 'hidden choice between both odds' is the sibling index; A/2 exists iff the lower rung
  is a genuine T-odd; the relaxation E-SCC is the ladder extended one rung down.

