A7  The equivalence theorem, checked
==============================================================================
Theorem 1 (PROVED in the note): R := closure of {1,2} under D and guarded E equals the T-basin of {1,2};
hence Collatz (every n >= 1 reaches 1) iff R = Z_{>0}.  Checks:
  (i) every n <= 1000000 reaches {1,2} under T (descent to an already-resolved smaller value).
  (ii) the D/E-closure of {1,2} inside [1, 10^5] contains exactly the n <= 3000 whose T-orbit
       stays <= 10^5 (2964 of 3000; the others peak above the cap, e.g. [703, 937, 1055, 1249, 1406, 1407]).
  (iii) functional graph: every node has exactly one parent T(n); by (i) the only cycle meeting
        [1, 10^6] is {1,2} (E(2) = 1 and D(1) = 2 are its two edges).

