  individual roots scatter strongly with their 3-adic expansion (Wirsching's s_n(a) is unbounded on a
  dense set of 3-adic a).  Small minus-sheet roots sit inside one of the three basins, so their trees
  are capped by 0.327, 0.3245 or 0.348: SHEET appears only at the small end.  Near the root cycle the model
  fails by an order-one factor (tree(4) = all n >= 3 on the plus sheet: rho = 4/R = 0.575): that is the
  archimedean boundary, where carries are as large as the values.

==============================================================================
K4  Incongruent (undecided) classes mod 3*2^k
==============================================================================
A class (n mod 3, parity word of length k) is DECIDED if the class determines a certificate of
multiplier < 1.  Three certificate sets:
  (I)   forward only: some prefix j <= k with 3^(a_j) < 2^j (Terras).  The mod-3 digit plays no role.
  (II)  owner-refined: (I), or n = 2 mod 3 (E(n) = (2n-1)/3 < n), or an even step j-1 -> j with
        T^j(n) = 2 mod 3 and (2/3) 3^(a_j)/2^j < 1 (the 'A/2 branch' E(T^j n) = (T^(j-1) n - 1)/3).
  (III) minimal-chain refined: (II), plus at every window point the non-retracing predecessor branch
        followed along its minimal-child chain for as many E-steps as the class determines
        (T^j(n) is known mod 3^(1+a_j): odd steps MANUFACTURE 3-adic precision).
  DP counts agree with brute force over all classes mod 3*2^k for k <= 12.

